      "content": "Do not give your child salt tablets, as this can dangerously increase their blood pressure and sodium levels, especially when they are already dehydrated. The safest way to rehydrate a toddler at night is to offer small, frequent sips of an oral rehydration solution like Pedialyte or plain water rather than plain water alone. If your child continues to refuse fluids, shows a very weak stream, or becomes lethargic, you should call your pediatrician immediately or go to the ER.",
